# <%= projectName %>

A [Furin](https://teyik0.github.io/furin/) app: React pages rendered by an Elysia server on Bun.

## Commands

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `bun install` | Install dependencies |
| `bun dev` | Start the dev server with HMR at http://localhost:3000 |
| `bun run build` | Build a self-contained executable in `.furin/build/bun/` |
| `bun run start` | Run the built executable |
| `bun run tscheck` | Type-check the project |
| `bun run fix` | Format and lint with Ultracite |

## Project layout

- `src/server.ts`: the Elysia app. API routes and the `furin()` plugin live here.
- `src/pages/`: file-based routes. `root.tsx` is the document layout; every other page exports `route`.
- `src/api/`: server code shared by API routes and page loaders.
- `public/`: files served as-is.

## Which config file owns what

- `bunfig.toml`: dev server. `[serve.static] plugins` must list `@teyik0/furin/strip-plugin` (and `bun-plugin-tailwind`) so Bun can bundle pages for the browser.
- `furin.config.ts`: production build (`furin build`). Bundler plugins used in production go here.
- `tsconfig.json`: TypeScript settings.
- `biome.jsonc`: lint and format rules used by `bun run fix`.
<% if (features.includes("shadcn")) { -%>
- `components.json`: shadcn/ui settings for `bunx shadcn add <component>`.
<% } -%>

## Type generation

`furin-env.d.ts` is generated by Furin. Despite its name, it does not type environment variables. It does two things:

- registers every page route, so `<Link to>`, `navigate()`, route params and `getRouteApi()` are type-checked;
- references Furin's ambient types for CSS and image imports.

Furin rewrites it when the dev server starts and when pages change, so do not edit it by hand. Keep it committed so `bun run tscheck` works on a fresh clone.

## Deployment

- Bun: `bun run build` produces `.furin/build/bun/server`, a single executable with assets embedded. Use `furin build --target bun` for a `server.js` bundle instead.
- Vercel: run `furin build --target vercel` and deploy `.vercel/output`. `src/server.ts` already exports the app and only listens when run directly, as Vercel requires.
- Static hosting: `furin build --target static` when every page uses `ssg`.

See the [deployment guide](https://teyik0.github.io/furin/docs/deployment) for details.
